  "title": "PROXY: Use a CONVERSATION_PROXY type",
  "description": "We set the packet to use a different conversation when looking up\nthe conversation and attaching a dissector to the packet, so that\na conversation dissector set by, e.g., HTTP, doesn't interfere with\nthe conversation dissector set by PROXY. Use a conversation type for\nproxy instead of the port type.\n\nThis avoids in a rare (illegal?) situation having an infinite loop\nof the PROXY dissector calling itself (through the TCP dissector).\n\nFix #20111",
